From bf59b6f5688f6fdf4de2955d1ba15f22f91636a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Franklin <cfranklin4474@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:29:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] mm/tier_ext: victim nomination (pick_victims) and
 lifecycle events

Let a tier_ext policy choose what to reclaim, not only judge what the
kernel's scanner presents. Before the engine (classic LRU or MGLRU) scans
an lruvec, pick_victims is asked for victims in batches of up to 32
folios. The policy nominates page frame numbers with the kfunc
bpf_tier_ext_add_victim(); the kernel trusts none of them: each pfn must
be an online head page on this lruvec's LRU, which is then isolated and
reclaimed through shrink_folio_list() as usual (folio_reclaim still
applies, with TIER_EXT_RC_NOMINATED). Nominated folios that are not
reclaimed are handed back through folio_added with TIER_EXT_F_RETURNED.
The pages the victims consumed are taken out of the engine's scan budget;
what the policy does not cover is reclaimed by the engine as before, and
at priority 0 the engine always gets its full budget.

A policy may return TIER_EXT_AGE to have MGLRU run its page table aging
for the lruvec (at most once per pass).

New events for policies that keep per-pfn state:
  folio_removed     freed without reclaim (__page_cache_release)
  folio_migrated    old pfn -> new pfn (migrate_folio_move)
  folio_referenced  MGLRU found young PTEs (walk_update_folio)
  folio_added       now also for THP split tails (TIER_EXT_F_SPLIT)
and a data_key in the folio context that identifies the data (file
offset or swap slot) independent of the page frame, including at
eviction, for ghost lists and refault detection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
